  "question": {
    "text": "Half lives of two radioactive nuclei <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> are 10 minutes and 20 minutes, respectively. If, initially a sample has equal number of nuclei, then after 60 minutes, the ratio of decayed numbers of nuclei A and B will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Half-life of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> : <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> minutes <br/>Number of half-lives in 60 minutes are: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>  <br/><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> Number of decayed nuclei of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>  <br/><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math>  <br/>Similarly, Half-life of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> : <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> minutes <br/>Number of half-lives of B in 60 minutes are: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>  <br/><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Number of decayed nuclei of B <br/><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math>  <br/><math><mo>∴</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn></math>"
  }
